{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\ncfg=json.loads(Path('build-config.json').read_text());p=Path(cfg['folder'])\n(p/'README.md').write_text('''# Orbit Invadettes\n\nOpen the single HTML in the parent directory directly in a browser. It contains the pristine Hub client, full pinned engine, all original sprite data, synthesized audio and game code. It needs no network in standalone play.\n\n- Move: A/D or arrows, stick/D-pad, or a horizontal mouse target.\n- Hold fire: Space, left mouse, R2 or Cross.\n- Repair nearest bunker: Q, right mouse, L1 or Square.\n- Pause/options: Escape or Options.\n- P2 on a shared keyboard: arrows, period to fire, slash to repair, Backspace to pause.\n- Touch: drag horizontally to move, clear lanes auto-fire, second contact intentionally cuts cover, temporary repair button spends salvage.\n\nLocal co-op is simultaneous. AI Hub provides online shared-world sessions; this file does not create standalone online rooms.\n\n## Build and verify\n\nFrom this directory:\n\n\"'```sh\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs\n```\n\nBuild requires the already installed Bun executable. Verification uses Node and the installed Python Playwright1.63.0 environment. Browsers are already present; the suite does not install any. The one verification command prints only failures and one aggregate count, with details in evidence/. It starts an owned loopback server on an OS-selected port only for Hub verification and closes its browsers/server afterward.\n\nThe native engine and Hub client are pinned in vendor/. Upstream engine is unchanged; full license is retained in the exported HTML. Read research/RESEARCH.md for inspected source evidence and limits; src/*-CONTRACT.md for simulation, assets/audio and shared authority.\n\nBalance values and six authored formations live in src/content.js. Pause → Developer tools exposes all encounters, both flagship phases, deterministic seeds, resource/deployment tools, diagnostics, time/step controls and live balance sliders. Changing a world marks it assisted; ordinary and assisted local records have separate views. Hub disables local world mutations.\n\nThe exact exit-interview.json at the parent root mirrors report.json, which is bundled into the in-game paged About/Credits.\n'\"''')\nf=Path('PROGRESS.md');s=f.read_text()+'''\\\\n## Acceptance checkpoint\\\\n- Hub integration:17 unit checks and63 live browser checks pass on pinned harness. One/two seats,150ms latency+jitter+5%loss,host-leave,server,remote repair/death/protected respawn,overlay,terminal agreement and stopped lifecycle covered. Largest measured full packet7279 bytes.\\\\n- Native actual-bundle headless checks:18 pass, including every encounter/phase rendering, local lifecycle, native solo/two-pad seat reclamation and2x single repair edge.\\\\n- Browser acceptance is running across Chromium/Firefox/WebKit, isolated file export, emulated phone/tablet/pads, audio signal/mute, storage, dev/attract and screenshots.\\\\n- Fixed additional issues: native audio/accessibility setting name mismatch; solo pad=null disabled discovery; duplicate native touch START overlapping custom pause;2x repair repeated edge; pose timing; breach wording; flagship wing geometry; safe-lane width; reduced-flash sprites; controller focus scrolling; P2 movement cancelling P1 pointer target; ordinary/assisted record views separated. Final unique issue count will be consolidated from actual logs.\\\\n- Remaining: final visual inspection, any browser fixes, final report/exit-interview, build and quiet aggregate test of exact export.\\\\n''';f.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\ncfg=json.loads(Path('build-config.json').read_text());p=Path(cfg['folder'])\n(p/'README.md').write_text('''# Orbit Invadettes\n\nOpen the single HTML in the parent directory directly in a browser. It contains the pristine Hub client, full pinned engine, all original sprite data, synthesized audio and game code. It needs no network in standalone play.\n\n- Move: A/D or arrows, stick/D-pad, or a horizontal mouse target.\n- Hold fire: Space, left mouse, R2 or Cross.\n- Repair nearest bunker: Q, right mouse, L1 or Square.\n- Pause/options: Escape or Options.\n- P2 on a shared keyboard: arrows, period to fire, slash to repair, Backspace to pause.\n- Touch: drag horizontally to move, clear lanes auto-fire, second contact intentionally cuts cover, temporary repair button spends salvage.\n\nLocal co-op is simultaneous. AI Hub provides online shared-world sessions; this file does not create standalone online rooms.\n\n## Build and verify\n\nFrom this directory:\n\n\"'```sh\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs\n```\n\nBuild requires the already installed Bun executable. Verification uses Node and the installed Python Playwright1.63.0 environment. Browsers are already present; the suite does not install any. The one verification command prints only failures and one aggregate count, with details in evidence/. It starts an owned loopback server on an OS-selected port only for Hub verification and closes its browsers/server afterward.\n\nThe native engine and Hub client are pinned in vendor/. Upstream engine is unchanged; full license is retained in the exported HTML. Read research/RESEARCH.md for inspected source evidence and limits; src/*-CONTRACT.md for simulation, assets/audio and shared authority.\n\nBalance values and six authored formations live in src/content.js. Pause → Developer tools exposes all encounters, both flagship phases, deterministic seeds, resource/deployment tools, diagnostics, time/step controls and live balance sliders. Changing a world marks it assisted; ordinary and assisted local records have separate views. Hub disables local world mutations.\n\nThe exact exit-interview.json at the parent root mirrors report.json, which is bundled into the in-game paged About/Credits.\n'\"''')\nf=Path('PROGRESS.md');s=f.read_text()+'''\\\\n## Acceptance checkpoint\\\\n- Hub integration:17 unit checks and63 live browser checks pass on pinned harness. One/two seats,150ms latency+jitter+5%loss,host-leave,server,remote repair/death/protected respawn,overlay,terminal agreement and stopped lifecycle covered. Largest measured full packet7279 bytes.\\\\n- Native actual-bundle headless checks:18 pass, including every encounter/phase rendering, local lifecycle, native solo/two-pad seat reclamation and2x single repair edge.\\\\n- Browser acceptance is running across Chromium/Firefox/WebKit, isolated file export, emulated phone/tablet/pads, audio signal/mute, storage, dev/attract and screenshots.\\\\n- Fixed additional issues: native audio/accessibility setting name mismatch; solo pad=null disabled discovery; duplicate native touch START overlapping custom pause;2x repair repeated edge; pose timing; breach wording; flagship wing geometry; safe-lane width; reduced-flash sprites; controller focus scrolling; P2 movement cancelling P1 pointer target; ordinary/assisted record views separated. Final unique issue count will be consolidated from actual logs.\\\\n- Remaining: final visual inspection, any browser fixes, final report/exit-interview, build and quiet aggregate test of exact export.\\\\n''';f.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"The game and product flows are in place, including separate assisted records, replay, attract play and live developer controls. Native engine checks pass for every encounter and both boss phases. I’m finishing the exact-export tests and visual review, particularly touch overlap, controller focus and telegraph readability.\n"}}
