{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path(json.loads(Path('build-config.json').read_text())['folder'])\nissues=[\n ('Moderate','Repair rebuilt adjacent cover into the missile radius at a cell boundary.','Simulation boundary regression'),\n ('Critical','ES-module export syntax was embedded in a classic script and prevented boot.','Native actual-bundle VM boot'),\n ('Moderate','Hub diagnostics were called as a function instead of read as an object.','Hub integration code review'),\n ('Moderate','A repair edge was repeated on both simulation substeps at 2× dev time.','Native 2× repair regression'),\n ('Minor','March pose changed every four steps instead of every step.','Native animation contract review'),\n ('Moderate','Breach defeat was labelled as exhausted deployments.','Simulation/UI cause review'),\n ('Moderate','Flagship art extent did not connect to the authoritative emitter positions.','Geometry contract and screenshot review'),\n ('Moderate','Flagship safe-lane preview was narrower than its actual safe width.','Telegraph contract review'),\n ('Moderate','Audio/accessibility controls used undefined engine setting names.','Browser settings checks and engine API review'),\n ('Critical','Solo/title pad=null disabled native gamepad discovery.','Native standardized gamepad regression'),\n ('Moderate','Native touch START overlapped the custom pause control.','Portrait phone screenshot inspection'),\n ('Moderate','Enemy-hit and respawn flashes ignored reduced-flash preference.','Native rendering contract review'),\n ('Moderate','Controller focus could leave controls clipped in scrollable panels.','Small-screen focus layout review'),\n ('Moderate','P2 movement cancelled the P1 mouse movement target.','Local seat input-routing review'),\n ('Moderate','Assisted and ordinary records initially shared the same view.','Records requirement review'),\n ('Moderate','Touch clicks changed the active modality to pointer and showed the wrong controls.','Browser touch controls assertion'),\n ('Moderate','Hyphenated boss/saucer events lacked their intended sound and effect routing.','Hub presentation audit and native event regression'),\n ('Moderate','Victory retained an intact flagship and skipped the planetary celebration.','Terminal presentation audit'),\n ('Minor','Missed salvage disappeared without a visible expiry warning or event.','Pickup lifecycle presentation audit'),\n ('Minor','Dedicated server application sampled local controls even though authority ignored them.','Hub server ownership audit'),\n ('Moderate','Adjusting a range control by gamepad changed the prompt family to keyboard.','Menu input provenance audit'),\n ('Moderate','Back/cancel was ignored while the developer seed text field had focus.','Controller menu navigation audit'),\n ('Moderate','Spent emitter boxes stayed behind when the phase-two flagship moved.','Flagship phase-two screenshot inspection')]\n(p/'evidence/ISSUES.md').write_text('# Unique issues found and fixed\\\\n\\\\nAll issues below have been fixed. Repeated failures from the same cause count once. Test pilot timing/modality mistakes are not game defects and are excluded. Contract and manual visual reviews are included alongside automated checks.\\\\n\\\\n'+ '\\\\n'.join(f'{i}. **{sev} / fixed** — {desc} Caught by: {test}.' for i,(sev,desc,test) in enumerate(issues,1))+'\\\\n\\\\nTotal: 23 unique issues, including 2 critical boot/control defects. Physical controller feel, human listening, actual TV distance and real iOS behavior remain unknown.\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
