{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/evidence/native-engine-review.md'; cat 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/evidence/hub-audit.json'\"","aggregated_output":"# Native engine verification and contract review\n\nThe actual shipped game.bundle.js is evaluated as a classic script in a Node VM after the full pinned engine, without stripping or transforming exports. The app uses the engine's supported headless renderer (`draw:true`). Native Input, fixed updates, draw, settings and lifecycle are exercised. DOM menus use explicit focus-row stand-ins for input routing; browser verification is still responsible for real focus/hit targets/layout.\n\n`tests/engine.test.mjs` exports asynchronous `runEngineTests()` and currently has18 passing checks. Includes one repair edge at2× simulation speed consuming exactly one charge, every encounter/phase rendering, local2-seat controls, pause/settings/dev/reset/replay, attract threshold/loop/wake isolation, record ownership, About feedback pages and no engine warnings/errors.\n\nDistinct findings delivered to root:\n\n1. **Critical / fixed** — Bun's default ESM output retained `export { App }` but final HTML loaded it through a classic `<script>`. Native boot failed with `SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'export'`, which also prevents browser startup. Build now explicitly requests IIFE output. Caught by executing the exact bundle in the native VM.\n2. **Moderate / fixed** — March animations passed beat×0.125 to2fps assets, changing pose once per four march beats. Contract review corrected this to beat×0.5 for alternating poses on every beat.\n3. **Moderate / fixed** — Results checked reason==='breach', while simulation returns a descriptive uppercase BREACH reason. Review corrected case-insensitive matching so breach defeat is identified correctly.\n4. **Moderate / fixed** —2× simulation scaling reused repair:true across both substeps and could spend two charges for one edge. Root neutralizes repair after the first substep; the native engine regression test verifies exactly one charge and one repair.\n5. **Moderate / fixed** —70px flagship hull was smaller than its148px collision width and placed emitter centers outside the pictured body. Root scales the native hull by2 to match its combat silhouette.\n6. **Moderate / fixed** — Phase-two SAFE box was44px wide while authoritative safeWidth is82px. Review aligned the telegraph box with boss.safeWidth.\n7. **Moderate / fixed by root** — Native sprite palette flashes and respawn alpha blinking bypassed the reduced-flash setting. Root gated these local effects on settings.flashes; updated native suite passes without errors. Browser/visual verification of their appearance belongs to root.\n\n8. **Critical / fixed** — Solo launch and return-to-title set Input.pad=null, which explicitly disables native gamepad polling. Root changed the selector to any and preserves claimed P2 exclusions. Native standard-mapping pad regressions verify combat, removal, reclaim, title confirmation, and distinct two-pad seats.\n\nCount these unique findings once when assembling combined feedback. Items1 and8 are critical native-engine findings. Root may already have the pad finding in its combined browser issue log; count it only once. Static contract review findings are identified separately from assertion failures; avoid claiming every item was discovered by automated play.\n{\n  \"scope\": \"Hub integration and read-only app/view/UI acceptance review\",\n  \"uniqueFindings\": 9,\n  \"criticalFindings\": 1,\n  \"automaticallyReproducedProductDefects\": 1,\n  \"notes\": \"Eight additional findings came from direct source-contract review. This is not a claim that nine automated tests failed. Export syntax and audio event mismatches were also seen by other team members and must be counted only once in a combined issue ledger. A test-fixture expectation adjustment is not a product defect.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"export-esm-in-classic-script\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\n      \"method\": \"Pinned live Hub harness startup test\",\n      \"finding\": \"Final bundled classic script contained export syntax, producing Unexpected token export and preventing hello/readiness.\",\n      \"status\": \"Fixed by root using Bun IIFE export; live harness then passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hub-diagnostics-object-call\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"method\": \"Source integration review\",\n      \"finding\": \"App debug snapshot and dev summary called adapter diagnostics() although the contract exposes diagnostics as an object.\",\n      \"status\": \"Fixed by root.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hyphenated-combat-presentation-events\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"method\": \"Source event-producer/consumer review; independent research agent also found audio mismatch\",\n      \"finding\": \"boss-hit, boss-phase, emitter-break and saucer-hit were absent from audio aliases and visual event routing, losing corresponding hit/destruction/phase feedback.\",\n      \"status\": \"Audio fixed by research agent; view fixed by root. Native asset/audio regression now covers exact simulation event names and throttling.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"victory-presentation-missing\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"method\": \"Source lifecycle and renderer review\",\n      \"finding\": \"Victory immediately opened results and continued drawing the intact hp0 flagship, omitting defended-planet celebration.\",\n      \"status\": \"Root added 2.4-second standalone planet/fireworks sequence and hides defeated hull.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"salvage-expiry-invisible\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"method\": \"Source simulation/render event review\",\n      \"finding\": \"Pickup life was never rendered and pickup-expire was ignored, so missed salvage disappeared without warning or expiry feedback.\",\n      \"status\": \"Root added warning indicator and expiry burst.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"server-local-input-sampling\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"method\": \"Source Hub server contract review\",\n      \"finding\": \"Server controller ignored input correctly, but the app still polled pads and sampled game.players before handing it to the adapter.\",\n      \"status\": \"Root skips app local input sampling on server sessions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"synthetic-slider-glyph-switch\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"method\": \"Source input provenance review\",\n      \"finding\": \"Controller range changes dispatch synthetic input; its listener forced activity(keyboard), switching prompts despite pad interaction.\",\n      \"status\": \"Root changed listener to preserve existing primary device.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"seed-field-back-ignored\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"method\": \"Source controller menu flow review\",\n      \"finding\": \"Dev text seed input continued before cancel/back handling, making Escape/Circle ineffective while that row had focus.\",\n      \"status\": \"Root handles cancel before the text-input editing skip.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hub-void-misreported-as-depleted-lives\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"method\": \"Source terminal lifecycle review\",\n      \"finding\": \"Non-finished Hub end reasons can leave shared world status playing; generic results therefore falsely said all deployments were exhausted after host-left/void/sat-out/session-ended.\",\n      \"status\": \"Fixed by root: onEnd retains sessionEndReason and non-finished Hub results show ROUND VOID / ROUND CLOSED with truthful explanation; authoritative world remains unchanged.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verification\": {\n    \"sessionUnitChecks\": 17,\n    \"sessionUnitFailures\": 0,\n    \"liveHubChecks\": 63,\n    \"liveHubFailures\": 0,\n    \"largestMeasuredSnapshotBytes\": 7279,\n    \"audioEventRegression\": \"Passed: exact boss-hit/core, boss-phase/heavy, emitter-break/heavy, saucer-hit/extra routes and repeated-core throttling.\",\n    \"physicalController\": \"unknown\",\n    \"humanListening\": \"unknown\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'spawnSaucer|y:28|y:26|saucer.y' 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/src/sim.js'; sed -n '125,175p' 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/src/sim.js'; cat 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/evidence/browser.json' | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'spawnSaucer|y:28|y:26|saucer.y' 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/src/sim.js'; sed -n '125,175p' 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/src/sim.js'; cat 'Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/evidence/browser.json' | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"139:export function spawnSaucer(w) {\n140: if(w.saucer)return false;const dir=w.volleyCount%2===0?1:-1;w.saucer={id:++w.entitySeq,x:dir>0?-20:500,y:28,dir,age:0,value:[100,200,300][Math.floor(random(w)*3)]};event(w,'saucer',{x:w.saucer.x,y:28 [... omitted end of long line]\n149: if(!w.saucer){w.saucerTimer-=dt;if(w.saucerTimer<=0){spawnSaucer(w);w.saucerTimer=28;}return;}\n195:   if(w.saucer)consider('saucer',w.saucer,sweepY(shot.x,oldY,newY,shot.r,w.saucer.x-12,w.saucer.y-4,w.saucer.x+12,w.saucer.y+4));\nfunction enemyAttacks(w,dt) {\n const d=WAVES[w.encounter];\n for(const e of w.enemies){e.flash=Math.max(0,e.flash-dt);if(e.shotPending){e.telegraph-=dt;if(e.telegraph<=0){e.telegraph=0;e.shotPending=false;addBomb(w,e.x,e.y+7,e.attackKind);}}}\n w.fireTimer-=dt;if(w.fireTimer>0||w.encounterTime<3.2)return;\n const active=w.players.filter(p=>p.active).length;const extra=active>1?1:0;\n let exposed=exposedEnemies(w).filter(e=>!e.shotPending);const parity=w.volleyCount%2;\n const preferred=exposed.filter(e=>e.col%2===parity);if(preferred.length)exposed=preferred;\n // Fisher-Yates on an authored exposed-column subset, with a serialized PRNG.\n for(let i=exposed.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(random(w)*(i+1));[exposed[i],exposed[j]]=[exposed[j],exposed[i]];}\n const count=Math.min(exposed.length,d.volley+extra,w.bullets.filter(b=>b.owner<0).length>=7?0:3);\n for(let i=0;i<count;i++){const e=exposed[i];e.shotPending=true;e.attackKind=e.type==='bombardier'?'heavy':'bomb';e.telegraph=d.telegraph+(e.type==='bombardier'?0.3:0);event(w,'telegraph',{x:e.x,y:e.y,kind:e.attackKind,duration:e.telegraph});}\n w.volleyCount++;w.fireTimer=w.tuning.fireInterval*d.fire;\n if(w.volleyCount%d.recoveryEvery===0)w.fireTimer+=d.recoveryFor;\n}\nexport function spawnSaucer(w) {\n if(w.saucer)return false;const dir=w.volleyCount%2===0?1:-1;w.saucer={id:++w.entitySeq,x:dir>0?-20:500,y:28,dir,age:0,value:[100,200,300][Math.floor(random(w)*3)]};event(w,'saucer',{x:w.saucer.x,y:28});return true;\n}\nexport function spawnEnemy(w,type='ordinary') {\n if(w.encounter>=6)return false;type=['ordinary','armour','bombardier'].includes(type)?type:'ordinary';\n let row=0,col=0;for(let r=0;r<4;r++)for(let c=0;c<8;c++)if(!w.enemies.some(e=>e.row===r&&e.col===c)){row=r;col=c;break;}\n if(w.enemies.some(e=>e.row===row&&e.col===col))return false;\n const hp=type==='armour'?2:1;w.enemies.push({id:++w.entitySeq,row,col,x:0,y:0,type,hp,maxHp:hp,telegraph:0,flash:0,shotPending:false,attackKind:'bomb'});w.formation.initial=Math.max(w.formation.initial,w.enemies.length);positions(w);return true;\n}\nfunction updateSaucer(w,dt) {\n if(!w.saucer){w.saucerTimer-=dt;if(w.saucerTimer<=0){spawnSaucer(w);w.saucerTimer=28;}return;}\n const s=w.saucer;s.age+=dt;s.x+=s.dir*31*dt;s.y=28+Math.sin(s.age*5)*1.5;\n if(s.x<-24||s.x>504){pickup(w,clamp(s.x,40,440),34,'saucer-trail');w.saucer=null;}\n}\nfunction bossStep(w,dt) {\n const b=w.boss;if(!b)return;b.age+=dt;b.phaseTime+=dt;b.hit=Math.max(0,b.hit-dt);\n if(b.phase===1){b.x=240+Math.sin(b.age*0.38)*94;for(let i=0;i<2;i++){const e=b.emitters[i];e.x=b.x+(i===0?-48:48);e.y=b.y+8;e.open=e.hp>0&&((b.phaseTime+i*2.5)%5)<3.2;e.telegraph=e.hp>0&&b.attackPending&&b.cycle%2===i?b.telegraph:0;}\n  b.open=false;\n }else{const target=clamp(b.safeLane,86,394);b.x+=clamp(target-b.x,-45*dt,45*dt);b.open=(b.phaseTime%6)>1.1&&(b.phaseTime%6)<4.9;}\n b.attackTimer-=dt;\n if(b.attackTimer<=0&&!b.attackPending){b.attackPending=true;b.telegraph=b.phase===1?1.0:1.35;b.cycle++;\n  if(b.phase===2)b.safeLane=48+96*((b.cycle*2+2)%5);\n  event(w,'telegraph',{x:b.phase===1?b.emitters[b.cycle%2].x:b.safeLane,y:b.y,kind:b.phase===1?'heavy':'lanes',duration:b.telegraph});\n }\n if(b.attackPending){b.telegraph-=dt;if(b.telegraph<=0){b.attackPending=false;b.telegraph=0;\n   if(b.phase===1){const side=b.cycle%2,x=b.emitters[side].x;for(const offset of [-22,0,22])addBomb(w,clamp(x+offset,24,456),b.y+18,offset===0?'heavy':'bomb');b.attackTimer=3.8;}\n   else{for(let x=24;x<=456;x+=36)if(Math.abs(x-b.safeLane)>b.safeWidth/2)addBomb(w,x,b.y+18,(x/36)%2===0?'heavy':'bomb');b.attackTimer=4.4;}\n  }\n }\n w.bossDropTimer-=dt;if(w.bossDropTimer<=0){pickup(w,48+384*random(w),112,'flagship');w.bossDropTimer=7;}\n}\n/** Parameter t of the first overlap of a vertical swept missile with a rectangle. */\nexport function sweepY(x,y,ny,r,left,top,right,bottom) {\n if(x+r<left||x-r>right)return null;top-=r;bottom+=r;\n if(y>=top&&y<=bottom)return 0;\n const dy=ny-y;if(dy>0&&y<top&&ny>=top)return (top-y)/dy;\n if(dy<0&&y>bottom&&ny<=bottom)return (bottom-y)/dy;\n      },\n      \"humanListening\": \"unverified\"\n    },\n    \"exceptions\": {\n      \"standard gamepads\": \"Traceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-022709__xc70359/work/Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/tests/browser.py\\\", line 58, in run\\n    fn()\\n    ~~^^\\n  File \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-022709__xc70359/work/Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022709/tests/browser.py\\\", line 1010, in <lambda>\\n    (\\\"standard gamepads\\\", lambda: suite.pads(browser)),\\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-022709__xc70359/work/Orbit-Invadettes-Astro-Battle-Space-Invaders-1979-gpt-6.